ateway gate. Residual caveat: consume-once duplicate handling is described only as serializing on the unique consume key without naming the stored record field returned, a documentation-level gap that does not reopen a trust boundary."},{"action":"present","contentHash":"sha256:f888cf9bb9788c9d5082c695858bbb17ba359b9a9a6b98d942041ecbcb4a89b2","evidenceId":"shadow-vote-assessment:sha256:8f1e39abb59756d4b9840f955e5d8c4b47f35d0934cd247735c0c65251f695bf","kind":"ARTIFACT","path":"/Users/ev/Projects/mihver/.project/run-bundles/authorization-ledger-v1c-r3-architecture-v7/evidence/shadow-vote-assessment-seat-openai-f888cf9bb9788c9d5082c695858bbb17ba359b9a9a6b98d942041ecbcb4a89b2.json","producedBy":{"role":"REVIEWER","threadId":null,"tool":"shadow-council-harness"},"sourcePath":"/Users/ev/Projects/mihver/.project/run-bundles/authorization-ledger-v1c-r3-architecture-v7/evidence/shadow-vote-assessment-seat-openai-f888cf9bb9788c9d5082c695858bbb17ba359b9a9a6b98d942041ecbcb4a89b2.json","summary":"The candidate satisfies the decisive V7 requirement: yesNoMatrix contains exactly 17 separately represented Q01–Q17 entries, including all distinct Claude/Codex pairs, with verbatim questions and NO answers. It also faithfully preserves decision-6’s privilege boundaries, atomic retry-safe stopEpoch protocol, exact-bound grants, dormant consume-once state, and zero V1C execution-effect consumers."}],"evidenceManifestHash":"sha256:ca8ced04d5896a78fd624d2867c0808affd21fd3a6041d994e00f0f7b44988d9"}
